{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-romans-006",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 6,
  "title": "Romans 6",
  "display_title": "Romans 6",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "romans",
  "book": "Romans",
  "bookName": "Romans",
  "bookOrder": 45,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 6,
  "sortOrder": 45006,
  "verseCount": 23,
  "aliases": [
    "Rom",
    "Ro",
    "Rm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "What shall we say then? Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "God forbid. How shall we, that are dead to sin, live any longer therein?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Know ye not, that so many of us as were baptized into Jesus Christ were baptized into his death?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Therefore we are buried with him by baptism into death: that like as Christ was raised up from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For if we have been planted together in the likeness of his death, we shall be also in the likeness of his resurrection:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Knowing this, that our old man is crucified with him, that the body of sin might be destroyed, that henceforth we should not serve sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For he that is dead is freed from sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Now if we be dead with Christ, we believe that we shall also live with him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Knowing that Christ being raised from the dead dieth no more; death hath no more dominion over him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For in that he died, he died unto sin once: but in that he liveth, he liveth unto God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Likewise reckon ye also yourselves to be dead indeed unto sin, but alive unto God through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Let not sin therefore reign in your mortal body, that ye should obey it in the lusts thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Neither yield ye your members as instruments of unrighteousness unto sin: but yield yourselves unto God, as those that are alive from the dead, and your members as instruments of righteousness unto God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under the law, but under grace.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "What then? shall we sin, because we are not under the law, but under grace? God forbid.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "But God be thanked, that ye were the servants of sin, but ye have obeyed from the heart that form of doctrine which was delivered you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Being then made free from sin, ye became the servants of righteousness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "I speak after the manner of men because of the infirmity of your flesh: for as ye have yielded your members servants to uncleanness and to iniquity unto iniquity; even so now yield your members servants to righteousness unto holiness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "For when ye were the servants of sin, ye were free from righteousness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "What fruit had ye then in those things whereof ye are now ashamed? for the end of those things is death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "But now being made free from sin, and become servants to God, ye have your fruit unto holiness, and the end everlasting life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:6:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 6:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:6:23"
      }
    }
  ],
